During the 1973–74 Scottish football season, [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] competed in [[Scottish Division One]].

Celtic won the league for the ninth season in a row, which was then a Scottish record, and has since been equaled by [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]] (1989-1997) and Celtic itself for a second time (2012-2020).

Celtic also won the Scottish Cup Final, defeating [[Dundee United F.C.|Dundee United]] 3-0, and narrowly missed on what would have been the club's third domestic treble as they lost the Scottish League Cup 1–0 to [[Dundee F.C.|Dundee FC]].

In European competition, Celtic made it to the semi-finals of the European Cup, where they fell to Spanish champions [[Atlético de Madrid]], 0–2 on aggregate. Previously, they had defeated Finnish champions [[Turun Palloseura|TPS]] 9–1 on aggregate, Danish champions [[Vejle Boldklub|Vejle]] 1–0 on aggregate, and Swiss champions [[FC Basel]] 6–5 on aggregate.

